l":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1946-04-23/pdf/FR-1946-04-23.pdf"},"source_id":"source-ladder:EO_9714:858e59926de7","status":"found_by_source_ladder"}],"signing_dates_seen":{"fr-originals@jobs/fr-originals/output":"1944-10-24","later-events_catalog":"1944-10-24","stage19_causal_queue":"1944-10-24"},"source_ladder_exhausted_proposed":[],"status":"MACHINE DRAFT - UNVERIFIED; not a claim; see jobs/claim-drafts/AGENT_GUIDE.md"},"claim":{"instrument_id":"EO:9492","later_source_search":[],"operative_clauses":[{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"1. The Secretary of War and the Secretary of the Navy are authorized and directed to permit transportation of non-military and non-naval passengers and cargo on Army air transports and Navy air transports operating over foreign routes, Provided:","original_source":{"page_or_item":"American Presidency Project web page (transcription; not an official edition); APP node 355129; common-crawl capture 2025-11-12T03:10:33Z; para. 1 (lead-in)","sha256":"c91110e68e8a127e1d9343539d5f65d888552efe95bc6997365c96b0d02a48fd","url":"https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/executive-order-9492-regulations-governing-non-military-and-non-naval-transportation-army"},"scope_id":"EO:9492#para1","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) That the transportation is certified by the War Department or the Navy Department as being in the national interest because it will contribute directly or indirectly to the war effort, or by the State Department, or the War or Navy Department acting for the State Department, as being in the national interest because it will similarly contribute (i) to relief or rehabilitation activities in areas affected by the war, or (ii) to the assumption of economic or other activities, disrupted by the war, that are necessary for the prompt reestablishment of peacetime conditions.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"American Presidency Project web page (transcription; not an official edition); APP node 355129; common-crawl capture 2025-11-12T03:10:33Z; para. 1(a)","sha256":"c91110e68e8a127e1d9343539d5f65d888552efe95bc6997365c96b0d02a48fd","url":"https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/executive-order-9492-regulations-governing-non-military-and-non-naval-transportation-army"},"scope_id":"EO:9492#para1(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) That the transportation is certified as being of such importance as to justify travel by air.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"American Presidency Project web page (transcription; not an official edition); APP node 355129; common-crawl capture 2025-11-12T03:10:33Z; para. 1(b)","sha256":"c91110e68e8a127e1d9343539d5f65d888552efe95bc6997365c96b0d02a48fd","url":"https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/executive-order-9492-regulations-governing-non-military-and-non-naval-transportation-army"},"scope_id":"EO:9492#para1(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"2. The Secretary of War and the Secretary of the Navy are authorized and directed to prescribe and administer appropriate regulations for their respective departments with respect to such transportation and priorities therefor, and such regulations shall include the following provisions","original_source":{"page_or_item":"American Presidency Project web page (transcription; not an official edition); APP node 355129; common-crawl capture 2025-11-12T03:10:33Z; para. 2 (lead-in)","sha256":"c91110e68e8a127e1d9343539d5f65d888552efe95bc6997365c96b0d02a48fd","url":"https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/executive-order-9492-regulations-governing-non-military-and-non-naval-transportation-army"},"scope_id":"EO:9492#para2","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) The air-transportation needs of the armed forces of this Government and of the United Nations for the war effort shall at all times have priority over non-military and non-naval needs for air transportation.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"American Presidency Project web page (transcription; not an official edition); APP node 355129; common-crawl capture 2025-11-12T03:10:33Z; para. 2(a)","sha256":"c91110e68e8a127e1d9343539d5f65d888552efe95bc6997365c96b0d02a48fd","url":"https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/executive-order-9492-regulations-governing-non-military-and-non-naval-transportation-army"},"scope_id":"EO:9492#para2(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) A reasonable charge (not less than the current commercial rates, if any, in tariffs on file with the Civil Aeronautics Board, for transportation and accommodations of a comparable nature between corresponding points) shall be made for the transportation, as authorized by this order, of non-military and non-naval passengers and cargo, other than such passengers and cargo carried for the War Department or the Navy Department.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"American Presidency Project web page (transcription; not an official edition); APP node 355129; common-crawl capture 2025-11-12T03:10:33Z; para. 2(b)","sha256":"c91110e68e8a127e1d9343539d5f65d888552efe95bc6997365c96b0d02a48fd","url":"https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/executive-order-9492-regulations-governing-non-military-and-non-naval-transportation-army"},"scope_id":"EO:9492#para2(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) No traffic other than military or naval traffic or traffic certified by the War Department or the Navy Department as contributing directly or indirectly to the war effort shall be carried if it can reasonably be handled by a United States civil air carrier, and all such traffic for which a charge is made, other than such traffic so certified as contributing to the war effort and lend-lease traffic, shall be terminated one year from the date of this order, or earlier on any given route if the Civil Aeronautics Board certifies that in its opinion commercial services of United States civil air carriers adequate to handle such traffic are in operation on such route.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"American Presidency Project web page (transcription; not an official edition); APP node 355129; common-crawl capture 2025-11-12T03:10:33Z; para. 2(c)","sha256":"c91110e68e8a127e1d9343539d5f65d888552efe95bc6997365c96b0d02a48fd","url":"https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/executive-order-9492-regulations-governing-non-military-and-non-naval-transportation-army"},"scope_id":"EO:9492#para2(c)","state_at_cutoff":null}],"original_representation":{"page_or_item":"9 FR 12859, PDF pages 1-2","sha256":"645f83a17166e026a33de70cb5f22b983bdf8c117cc5b61cc51788dea29e4346","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1944-10-27/pdf/FR-1944-10-27.pdf"},"research_rationale":"","savings_residuals":null,"schema":"eo-lifecycle-claim/v1","unresolved_material_gaps":["DRAFT: state_at_cutoff not decided for 7 clause(s); clause inventory completeness not confirmed","DRAFT: whole-order ending not established","DRAFT: savings and residual effects not closed","DRAFT: later_source_search not recorded (machine searches are proposals only; paste them after judging them adequate and resolving every CONFLICT line)"],"whole_order_end":null,"whole_order_status":"no"},"draft_schema":"eo-claim-draft/v1","instrument_id":"EO:9492"}
